    "scope": "Run all 2464 case/profile combinations from this manifest on each host. Each linked row requires fresh INT and AOT outcomes tied to the same guest, the threaded memory owner where applicable, and the host VM receipt. Each original upstream case and each SDK-authored case has its own row.",
    "threaded_budgets": {
      "find": "Four threaded MTE profiles add measured ELF relocation counts to the LLVM AOT per-child budget on Linux x86_64 and i686. The default per-thread Guest native stack is 1 MiB and per-child storage is 16 MiB.",
      "aot_stack": "The 15 original native-stack refusals determine the per-profile AOT stack sizes in the manifest. Round the required bytes of proven native frames plus 8192 bytes of observed guard pages up to the next whole MiB. The original interpreter runs passed these rows with 1 MiB."
    }
  },
  "successor_vm_commit": "08990a38a116cf09e79378e091b54551fa2ab763",
  "observations": [
    "The original lsearch program declares an 80-byte record and supplies shorter strings. The SDK port supplies full-width records.",
    "The upstream named semaphore fixture requires sem_unlink at link time. The unnamed semaphore companion ran on the eight threaded profiles.",
    "The original rwlock test imports poll_oneoff for sleep. The 03a3 harness denied this interface. The joined companion exercises completion independently.",
    "The threaded MTE libc++ find program exceeded the recorded per-child LLVM AOT relocation allowance in four x86_64 profiles.",
    "The upstream floatuntisf source printed its skip diagnostic on both engines."
  ],
